To incorporate the `HELP` and `RMD` client requests into the existing sequence of commands, we can place `HELP` after the `SYST` command, as it is a good practice to check for available commands or assistance after establishing the connection. The `RMD` (Remove Directory) command should come after the `LIST` command, as it makes sense to list the contents of the current directory before attempting to remove a directory.

Here’s the modified sequence of client requests:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
HELP
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
RMD <directory_name>  ; Replace <directory_name> with the actual directory you want to remove
QUIT
```

Make sure to replace `<directory_name>` with the actual name of the directory you wish to remove

